  "query_preview": "..\nToday through Monday...\n\nA much calmer weather pattern is expected over the next 7 days. \nTemperatures will increase today and Wednesday into the 45-55\ndegree range as weak 500 mb high pressure blocking sets up over \nthe region. Temperatures increase further Thursday through the \nend of the period as downsloping winds Friday transition to upper \nlevel ridging by Saturday. Temperatures are expected to increase \nfrom the 50s F Thursday through Saturday into the 55-65 degree \nrange Sunday and Monday. The next 7 days look dry with the only \nchance for precipitation coming Friday as a shortwave trough moves\nacross the Canadian border. Precipitation potential from this is \nlimited with models indicating 0.10 inches of precipitation at \nmost.\n\nThe most impactful weather in the coming days will be increasing\nwind potential for the foothills west of Billings starting\nThursday. The GFS is indicating that the Idaho Falls to Lewistown\npressure gradient will be around 9 mb Thursday morning but 700 mb\nwinds will be weak. Strong wind potential increases Friday through\nMonday due to persistent high pressure in Yellowstone National \nPark and elevated 700 mb winds. At this time, the chances for\nwinds to gust over 50 mph remain below 50%. Torgerson",
